title: Add live Codex E2E coverage for hooks+CLI and managed app-server transports
updated_at: "2026-07-12T03:19:11Z"
---
Current Codex coverage is split but incomplete: ocaml/cli/test_c2c_hook_codex.ml and the hook-fallback row in scripts/codex-draft-preservation-e2e.py invoke c2c hook codex directly with synthetic payloads, while scripts/codex-ingress-dogfood.py and scripts/codex-autoturn-e2e.py exercise app-server seams without launching the managed c2c start/new codex supervisor. Add two opt-in live E2E paths: (1) vanilla or C2C_CODEX_FORCE_HOOKS=1 Codex with isolated CODEX_HOME/config.toml installed hooks, a real peer DM, natural hook invocation, transcript additionalContext assertion, and inbox-drain assertion; (2) supported Codex launched through c2c start/new codex app-server supervision, peer DM, arrival-time model-visible injection, eligible local auto-turn, draft-preservation and teardown assertions. Gate on explicit credentials/version/live-test environment, keep default CI hermetic, and document/retire obsolete XML-sideband E2E references.

The hook-path E2E can reuse the existing herdr testing harness (or a close
variant): start a normal Codex process under herdr with the isolated hooks
configuration, rather than launching it through `c2c new codex` / `c2c start
codex`. This keeps the hook+CLI transport test distinct from the managed
app-server supervisor test while retaining realistic process and TTY behavior.
